value.CONCEPT_SKY_STYLE.CONCEPT_SKY_PHOTON_ORIGINAL = Photon Concept
option.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS                  = Enhanced Star Field
option.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS.comment          = A dense deep-space star field all around the End, the Void below the island included, bent and pulled by the black hole. Warm white, gold and orange stars with a few blue-white ones, and the nebula's young cluster: a knot of hot blue-white stars in its heart. Works with both sky styles. Off: Photon's original stars. Stars Coverage and Stars Intensity (Sky > Stars) set its density and brightness
option.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS_WORLD           = Star Field World
option.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS_WORLD.comment   = Which worlds the Enhanced Star Field appears in. In the Overworld it takes the place of Photon's stars at night and turns with the sky.
option.MILKY_WAY                             = Milky Way (Overworld)
option.MILKY_WAY.comment                     = A Milky Way band across the Overworld's night sky in our nebula's colours: an amber core, bluish ends, star clouds and a dark dust lane. Turns with the stars, shows only at night. Costs next to no performance.
option.MILKY_WAY_INTENSITY                   = Milky Way Intensity
option.MILKY_WAY_INTENSITY.comment           = How bright the Milky Way is, in percent.
suffix.MILKY_WAY_INTENSITY                   = %
value.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_END = End Only
value.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_OVERWORLD = Overworld Only
value.CONCEPT_ENHANCED_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_BOTH = Both
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS                     = Shooting Stars
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS.comment             = Now and then a bright streak crosses the End's sky, headed downwards, its tail fading behind it, and is gone in about a second. Costs next to no performance.
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS_FREQUENCY           = Shooting Star Frequency
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS_FREQUENCY.comment   = How often they appear, in percent (100%: roughly one every 3 to 7 seconds in the part of the sky you are looking at).
suffix.END_SHOOTING_STARS_FREQUENCY           = %
option.END_PORTAL_CONCEPT                     = Cinematic End Portal
option.END_PORTAL_CONCEPT.comment             = The End portal (and gateway) with Minecraft's own look - layers of small square specks - in our End's colours: a near-black base, specks in the nebula's orange, amber and blue, a few warm white ones like the black hole's disc, and a faint nebula cloud deep down. The layers sit at real depths (they move against each other as you walk), twinkle, and a few flare now and then. Off: Photon's portal.
option.END_PORTAL_GLOW                        = Portal Light and Mist
option.END_PORTAL_GLOW.comment                = The End portal lights the room in our End's warm light, and a mist in the nebula's colours (orange and blue) rises out of it, with glints rising and fading. Needs Colored Lights on. Costs some performance.
option.END_PORTAL_MIST_INTENSITY              = Portal Mist Intensity
option.END_PORTAL_MIST_INTENSITY.comment      = How strongly the portal's mist and glints show, in percent.
suffix.END_PORTAL_MIST_INTENSITY              = %
option.OVERWORLD_PLANET_MOON_SIZE             = Planet-Moon Size
option.OVERWORLD_PLANET_MOON_SIZE.comment     = How big the planet is in the sky, in percent of Photon's moon.
suffix.OVERWORLD_PLANET_MOON_SIZE             = %
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_WORLD                   = Black Hole World
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_WORLD.comment           = Which worlds the black hole appears in. In the Overworld it has the same place in the sky as in the End; by day it is fainter, behind the blue of the sky, as the moon is by day (it does not light the world).
option.END_PLANET_WORLD                       = Planet World
option.END_PLANET_WORLD.comment               = Which worlds the planet appears in. In the Overworld it is the moon: it rises and sets with it and has its phases (shader moon only, not Vanilla Moon).
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS_WORLD               = Shooting Stars World
option.END_SHOOTING_STARS_WORLD.comment       = Which worlds the shooting stars appear in. In the Overworld at night only, behind the clouds.
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_END   = End Only
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_OVERWORLD = Overworld Only
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_BOTH  = Both
value.END_PLANET_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_END       = End Only
value.END_PLANET_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_OVERWORLD = Overworld Only
value.END_PLANET_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_BOTH      = Both
value.END_SHOOTING_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_END = End Only
value.END_SHOOTING_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_OVERWORLD = Overworld Only
value.END_SHOOTING_STARS_WORLD.CONCEPT_WORLD_BOTH = Both

screen.concept_stars                           = Stars
screen.concept_stars.comment                   = The star field, the Milky Way and the shooting stars.
screen.end_black_hole                          = Black Hole
screen.end_black_hole_color                    = Black Hole Colour
screen.end_black_hole_color.comment            = Red, green and blue of the black hole's light
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_RAYS                    = Black Hole Rays
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_RAYS.comment            = The black hole's light coming through the air between the obsidian pillars, in beams: a thin haze round the main island, lit by it and shadowed by the pillars. Strongest looking towards it. Needs Environmental Light on. Costs little performance.
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_RAYS_INTENSITY          = Ray Intensity
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_RAYS_INTENSITY.comment  = How strongly the rays show, in percent.
suffix.END_BLACK_HOLE_RAYS_INTENSITY          = %
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_R                  = §c▍ §fRed
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_R.comment          = How much red the black hole's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of everything that is its own: the disc, the ring, the halo, the light it casts on the nebula and the light it casts on the world (blocks, fog, planet).
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_G                  = §a▍ §fGreen
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_G.comment          = How much green the black hole's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of everything that is its own: the disc, the ring, the halo, the light it casts on the nebula and the light it casts on the world (blocks, fog, planet).
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_B                  = §9▍ §fBlue
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_TINT_B.comment          = How much blue the black hole's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of everything that is its own: the disc, the ring, the halo, the light it casts on the nebula and the light it casts on the world (blocks, fog, planet).
option.END_BLACK_HOLE                          = Enabled
option.END_BLACK_HOLE.comment                  = Black hole with an accretion disc, bending the stars behind it. Currently shown in the End only
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_INTENSITY                = Intensity
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_INTENSITY.comment        = Overall strength of the black hole effect: from 0 to 1 it fades the whole effect in or out. Above 1 only its light gets stronger (for testing)
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_SIZE                     = Size
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_SIZE.comment             = Apparent size of the black hole in the sky
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_WARP_STRENGTH            = Gravitational Lensing
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_WARP_STRENGTH.comment    = Controls how strongly light bends around the black hole
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_DISC_BRIGHTNESS          = Disc Brightness
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_DISC_BRIGHTNESS.comment  = Controls the brightness of the accretion disc, and of the gold light it casts on the nebula's gas round it
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_BROAD_HALO              = Broad Halo
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_BROAD_HALO.comment      = Soft light spreading from the black hole far into the surrounding space, several times its size. It never lights the dark centre, and it is independent of Disc Brightness
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_LIGHT                    = Environmental Light
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_LIGHT.comment            = The black hole becomes the End's light source: terrain facing it is lit and everything casts shadows away from it, with Photon's shadow settings. Follows Intensity and Disc Brightness. Off: Photon's own End lighting
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_SPEED                    = Animation Speed
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_SPEED.comment            = Controls the speed of the accretion disc's swirling animation. The black hole's pull follows it too (0 stops everything); to change the pull alone, use Pull Speed
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL                     = Pull Speed
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL.comment             = How fast the black hole is seen pulling the sky in: the stars round it streaming into it and the nebula's gas falling towards it (the gas only with Nebula Motion on). It does not change the disc's animation or the rest of the nebula's motion. Off: nothing falls in, the stars round it only circle it
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL.0                    = Off
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL.1                    = Slow
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL.2                    = Normal
value.END_BLACK_HOLE_PULL.3                    = Fast
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_STEPS                    = Quality
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_STEPS.comment            = Raymarching step count for the accretion disc. Higher looks better but costs more performance
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_ELEVATION                = Elevation
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_ELEVATION.comment        = Height of the black hole above the horizon, in degrees. Low values put it near the horizon, 90 puts it straight overhead
suffix.END_BLACK_HOLE_ELEVATION                 = °
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_AZIMUTH                  = Azimuth
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_AZIMUTH.comment          = Compass direction of the black hole in degrees: 0 = north, 90 = east, 180 = south, 270 = west. Default 120 (east-southeast)
suffix.END_BLACK_HOLE_AZIMUTH                   = °
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_INCLINATION              = Disc Inclination
option.END_BLACK_HOLE_INCLINATION.comment      = How open the accretion disc looks. Low values show it edge-on (like a thin line), high values show it from above
suffix.END_BLACK_HOLE_INCLINATION               = °

screen.end_planet                              = Planet
option.END_PLANET                              = Enabled
option.END_PLANET.comment                      = A colossal planet on a wide orbit around the End's main island. Completely independent of the black hole: it can be used with the black hole off. Currently shown in the End only
option.END_PLANET_SIZE                         = Size
option.END_PLANET_SIZE.comment                 = Apparent size of the planet
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_AZIMUTH                = Orbit Azimuth
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_AZIMUTH.comment        = Compass direction the planet rises and sets in, in degrees: 0 = north, 90 = east, 180 = south, 270 = west
suffix.END_PLANET_ORBIT_AZIMUTH                 = °
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_INCLINATION            = Orbit Inclination
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_INCLINATION.comment    = How high the planet climbs at the top of its orbit, in degrees above the horizon
suffix.END_PLANET_ORBIT_INCLINATION             = °
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_RADIUS                 = Orbit Radius
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_RADIUS.comment         = Distance from the End island the planet orbits at, in blocks. Larger orbits shift less as you fly around the island
suffix.END_PLANET_ORBIT_RADIUS                  = m
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_THROUGH_BLACK_HOLE     = Orbit through Black Hole
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_THROUGH_BLACK_HOLE.comment = Turns the orbit so the planet passes right in front of the black hole once per lap, as seen from the main island (same size, inclination, radius and speed). Orbit Azimuth is not used while this is on. Needs the black hole in the same world
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_PHASE                  = Orbit Phase
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_PHASE.comment          = Where the planet is on its orbit when the game starts, in degrees. With Orbit through Black Hole: 0 = centred in front of the black hole, negative = still approaching it. Otherwise: 0 = where it rises. With Orbit Speed 0 the planet stays there
suffix.END_PLANET_ORBIT_PHASE                   = °
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_SPEED                  = Orbit Speed
option.END_PLANET_ORBIT_SPEED.comment          = How fast the planet travels around its orbit. Independent of the black hole's Animation Speed
option.END_PLANET_ROTATION_SPEED               = Rotation Speed
option.END_PLANET_ROTATION_SPEED.comment       = How fast the planet turns on its own axis. Independent of the black hole's Animation Speed

screen.end_nebula                              = Nebula
screen.end_nebula_sea_color                    = Sea Colour
screen.end_nebula_sea_color.comment            = Red, green and blue of the Nebula Sea's light (the sea of gas below the End)
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_R                  = §c▍ §fRed
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_R.comment          = How much red the Nebula Sea's light has (1.00: unchanged). The sea's colour is its own: Nebula Colour does not change the sea, and this does not change the rest of the nebula.
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_G                  = §a▍ §fGreen
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_G.comment          = How much green the Nebula Sea's light has (1.00: unchanged). The sea's colour is its own: Nebula Colour does not change the sea, and this does not change the rest of the nebula.
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_B                  = §9▍ §fBlue
option.END_NEBULA_SEA_TINT_B.comment          = How much blue the Nebula Sea's light has (1.00: unchanged). The sea's colour is its own: Nebula Colour does not change the sea, and this does not change the rest of the nebula.
screen.end_nebula_color                        = Nebula Colour
screen.end_nebula_color.comment                = Red, green and blue of the nebula's light (but for the Nebula Sea, which has its own colour)
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_R                      = §c▍ §fRed
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_R.comment              = How much red the nebula's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of all of it: lower one to take that colour out, raise it to strengthen it. All at 1.00: its own colours.
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_G                      = §a▍ §fGreen
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_G.comment              = How much green the nebula's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of all of it: lower one to take that colour out, raise it to strengthen it. All at 1.00: its own colours.
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_B                      = §9▍ §fBlue
option.END_NEBULA_TINT_B.comment              = How much blue the nebula's light has (1.00: unchanged). Together the three change the colour of all of it: lower one to take that colour out, raise it to strengthen it. All at 1.00: its own colours.
option.END_NEBULA_QUALITY                      = Nebula Quality
option.END_NEBULA_QUALITY.comment              = How many samples the nebula takes along each view ray, in percent. Lower: more frame rate (the nebula is the heaviest part of the End's sky), and a grainier nebula - which Frame Accumulation, on, averages away: down to about 60% the difference is hard to see. Its shapes stay the same.
suffix.END_NEBULA_QUALITY                      = %
option.END_NEBULA_TEMPORAL                     = Frame Accumulation
option.END_NEBULA_TEMPORAL.comment             = Averages the nebula over the last frames, following the camera, so its grain is gone - also while you walk, when the anti-aliasing alone lets it show and the nebula looks lower in resolution. Costs a little performance. Off: as before.
option.END_NEBULA                              = Nebula
option.END_NEBULA.comment                      = The Eagle Nebula (M16) in the Hubble palette, rebuilt from astronomical images: the island floats inside it. A cyan heart round its young star cluster, golden and amber clouds lit from it with bright orange edges where they face it, dark dust (pillars, lanes, a large dark cloud) and, in a few places, rust red. Next to the black hole, which sits on its golden clouds. One 3D volume thousands of blocks away, continued round the whole sky, below the island too, with black gaps, and a luminous sea of gas below the island, in the Void, climbing towards the heart. Works with both sky styles (violet in Photon Concept). Off: the End sky without it
option.END_NEBULA_INTENSITY                    = Nebula Intensity
option.END_NEBULA_INTENSITY.comment            = Brightness of the nebula's gas. From 0 to 1 it also fades its dark dust in or out
option.END_NEBULA_COVERAGE                     = Nebula Coverage
option.END_NEBULA_COVERAGE.comment             = How much of the sky outside the main nebula its gas covers: lower values leave larger black gaps, higher values smaller ones (default 1.00; up to 2.00 covers much more)
option.END_NEBULA_MOTION                       = Nebula Motion
option.END_NEBULA_MOTION.comment               = The nebula's gas streams towards the black hole: its clouds, the sea, the canopy and the close wisps all flow that way, each scale at its own speed so the clouds change shape as they go, and seen from the island the stream converges on the black hole. On top of that the fine detail expands away from the nebula's heart, follows large gusts and, near the black hole, falls towards it; round the black hole the far gas itself is seen falling into it, faster the closer it is, turning round it; thin fronts of brightness leave the heart and cross the clouds. The heart itself stays where it is. Slow, Normal and Fast set how fast. Off: static
value.END_NEBULA_MOTION.0                      = Off
value.END_NEBULA_MOTION.1                      = Slow
value.END_NEBULA_MOTION.2                      = Normal
value.END_NEBULA_MOTION.3                      = Fast
option.END_NEBULA_DUST                         = Cosmic Dust
option.END_NEBULA_DUST.comment                 = Tiny dust grains suspended in the space around you, at fixed places in the world: fine grains from about 12 blocks away and more from 50 to 300 blocks. The closest pass by quickly as you move and the farther ones slowly, like dust in the air after rain. They glow faintly and catch a little of the nebula's light behind them. Normal and Strong also thicken the nebula's own dust a little. Subtle, Normal and Strong set how many; Off turns them off. Strongest in the Cinematic Void, faint in Photon Concept
value.END_NEBULA_DUST.0                        = Off
value.END_NEBULA_DUST.1                        = Subtle
value.END_NEBULA_DUST.2                        = Normal
value.END_NEBULA_DUST.3                        = Strong
option.END_NEBULA_SEA                          = Nebula Sea
option.END_NEBULA_SEA.comment                  = A luminous sea of gas below the whole End, in the Void: a landscape under the island, all round it, cyan where the nebula's heart lights it and amber elsewhere, with relief, rising a little in the distance so it shows in every direction. It leaves a wide bay round the black hole. Off: only the nebula's clouds
option.END_NEBULA_CANOPY                       = Nebula Canopy
option.END_NEBULA_CANOPY.comment               = The Nebula Sea's sister layer, high in the End's sky: soft patches of cyan and amber gas behind the nebula's clouds, so the sky has the same composition as the Void below. Only high up, clear of the horizon, the black hole and the nebula's heart. Off: only the nebula's clouds in the sky
